de his first of many lasting  contributions to the marvel mythos as he  introduced the concept of captain  america's iconic  shield toss now not wanting to tarnish  his name by attaching it to a comic book  which  in truth were seen as a source of  entertainment for the masses and without  much artistic merit stan chose to write  the story under the pseudonym of stan  lee  figuring this would allow him to one day  begin writing novels under his real name  without the stigma of being a comic book  writer now when joe simon the editor of  timely comics had a falling out with  martin goodman he and his captain  america co-creator jack kirby left the  company and goodman turned to stan lee  to be the interim editor of timely in  1941.  now although he was only 19 stan  flourished in the role but in 1942  stan lee joined the army with the united  states in the midst of the second world  war lee listed playwright as his  occupation  upon entering the army and was able to  use his writing skills in crafting  manuals and scripts  for training films i really want to read  a world war ii stanley training manual  but interestingly lee shared a division  with another soldier who would become a  pop culture icon  theodore gesell who would later publish  legendary children's books  under the pen name dr seuss now  throughout his military service  stan would correspond with timely comics  who would send him assignments that he  would complete and mail back  going so far as to break into a mailbox  when his letters from timely were not  delivered on time which would have ended  with stan going to prison if not for the  influence of his commanding officer now  when lee's time in the military was over  he returned to timely and was able to  resume his role as editor and it was  around this time that stan's cousin set  him up on a date with john buccock who'd  been a hat model in britain before  moving to the us  now after only two weeks of dating stan  proposed to jones and the two were  married on december 5th  1947. now in 1950 stan's oldest daughter  jc was born and three years later his  youngest daughter jan was born and then  tragically died eight days later now  stan remained married to joan until her  death in 2017  at the age of 94. they lived a beautiful  life together now by this time  superhero comics had largely fallen out  of favor and so stan's writing  assignments were generally in the  romance and western genres which were  far more popular at the time now this  led to lee  becoming disenchanted with his career  throughout the 1950s at timely which had  since changed its name  to atlas now on the break of burning out  lee's wife joan advised him to just  start writing the stories he wanted to  write instead of what was most likely to  sell  however things were in motion that would  change the course of lee's life  forever sounds dramatic the first is  that superheroes had seen an increase in  popularity once again  due to some developments over at dc  comics the primary competitor to marvel  which i'm just going to be using marvel  comics to refer to the company that was  at various times timely atlas  marvel and so on but that name switched  to marvel was basically officially made  in 1961 but the other factor in stan  lee's rise was the return of artist  jack kirby to marvel comics in the 1950s  now with marvel desperate to counter the  success of dc superhero team the justice  league of america  lee and kirby were tasked with creating  a superhero team of their own and so lee  took his wife's advice to heart and set  out to make the type of story that he  would want to read  creating characters that were flawed and  more relatable than the infallible  superheroes that had dominated the pages  of comics  up to that point and so the fantastic  four the first of many collaborative  creations of lee and kirby were born now  as to the role that lee  and kirby would each play in the  creation of the characters that's a  source of 